    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #321\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch pushed successfully to `bb/relay-117-agent-runtime-02-08-push-live-run-even-thr_rx7w49ymgx`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #117: the live push hook and startup repair sweep that build on #228's `packages/agent-runtime` lifecycle adapter.\n\n**Live push hook** — `runAgentSession` now publishes every message it observes, including `message_update` streaming deltas, as a new `agent_run_event` realtime NOTIFY (`@semprec/realtime`'s `RealtimeMessage` union). This is best-effort (a failed publish is logged, never fails the run) and happens for every message kind, while persistence to `agent_run_events` still skips `message_update` — so deltas are observable live but absent from Postgres, per the acceptance criteria.\n\n**Startup repair sweep** — new `repairInterruptedRuns(pool)` exported from `@semprec/agent-runtime`, backed by a new `listRunningAgentRuns` query in `@semprec/data`. In one transaction it:\n1. Closes every `agent_runs` row still `status='running'` as `status='error'`, `finished_at=now()`, `result='interrupted_by_restart'`.\n2. For each such run whose last `agent_run_events` row is an unpaired `tool_use`, appends a synthetic `tool_result` (carrying over the original tool-call fields, marked `error: true`) so the transcript's tool-calling invariant holds.\n\nThis is a ready-to-call primitive; no `semprec-agents` service process exists yet in the repo to invoke it at boot or to wire the push into a live server, consistent with #228 also having no live caller yet.\n\n**Testing**: added integration tests for both the push hook (via a real LISTEN/NOTIFY round trip) and the repair sweep (orphan detection, synthetic tool_result insertion/non-insertion, no-op cases). Full suite verified in this session: build ✅, `check:boundaries` ✅, unit 83/83 ✅, integration 431/431 ✅, e2e 5/5 ✅.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
