    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #321\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed the code-review follow-up commit to the existing branch `bb/relay-117-agent-runtime-02-08-push-live-run-even-thr_rx7w49ymgx` (same branch backing PR #321).\n\n## Summary\n\nThis push addresses the CI code-review feedback on PR #321:\n\n- **High-severity fix**: `startupRepair.ts` no longer blindly casts the untyped JSONB `payload` to `Record<string, unknown>` — it now validates the value is a plain object first, falling back to `{}` for a malformed row instead of risking a runtime crash. Added a regression test with a non-object payload.\n- **Run-status push criterion**: the lifecycle adapter now also emits a `run_status` realtime event for the run's own lifecycle transitions (start → `running`, finish → `done`/`error`), on top of the mid-session `run_status` `AgentMessage` kind it already pushed — covering every live event category the issue lists. Deduplicated the publish-with-best-effort-catch logic into one helper.\n- **Flaky test fix**: replaced the fixed 50ms sleep waiting for NOTIFY delivery with a bounded poll loop, and extended assertions to cover the new `run_status` pushes.\n- **Startup-wiring criterion**: confirmed via the issue tracker that the actual `services/semprec-agents` composition root is issue #91's explicit deliverable (not #117's, and not yet built anywhere in the repo — `backend/services/` is still empty). Building a stand-in service now would risk conflicting with #91's real design. Instead, documented in `repairInterruptedRuns`'s docstring that #91 is the intended caller, ready to wire in once that composition root exists.\n\nVerified before pushing: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `check:boundaries` clean, full suite green — unit 83/83, integration 432/432, e2e 5/5.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
